yolo-v9-t-256-license-plates.onnx
  Status: since 2026-11-09 not built into the app or on its About page (plates-yolox-nano-256.onnx replaced it). All
        below is as it stood; the file and LICENSE-yolov9-plates stay in the tree for comparisons.
  What: YOLOv9-t licence plate detector (one class, 1.9 M parameters), 1x3x256x256 RGB 0..1 -> 1x5x1344 (centre x, y,
        width, height in input pixels, score after sigmoid; anchors of strides 8 / 16 / 32, row-major). It is the
        published yolo-v9-t-256-license-plates-end2end.onnx cut before its NMS by onnx.utils.Extractor at
        /model/model.22/Concat_5_output_0 (renamed "output"), nothing else changed: the source's producer fields
        (pytorch 2.3.1) are kept, which the sha256 below depends on (as the Extractor writes them, the same graph
        hashes 338bef273b8449253383b7088712720ae6fd1b003483de91280950f0181e4c4a). The end2end graph ends in
        Transpose, a MatMul (centre to corners) and NonMaxSuppression (IoU 0.45, score 0.001, 100 boxes per class)
        with Gathers to n x 7 (batch, x0, y0, x1, y1, class, score). burn-onnx 0.22 generates code for that NMS, but it
        needs burn's `vision` feature (whose NMS on cubecl reads boxes and scores back to the CPU per batch entry), and
        that feature's dependencies do not resolve in this workspace (burn-dataset, globwalk, aws-lc-rs missing from
        the local registry index), so the NMS runs in Rust (src/plates.rs, IoU 0.45 as the graph's). Plates are
        searched on square crops around YOLOX's vehicles (src/plates.rs `plate_crops`).
  Source: https://github.com/ankandrew/open-image-models, release "assets", the URL the package's hub.py downloads:
          https://github.com/ankandrew/open-image-models/releases/download/assets/yolo-v9-t-256-license-plates-end2end.onnx
          No checksum is published (GitHub's asset digest is empty for the 2024 uploads). sha256 of the download
          938a34ce868da69432fd5a872f24337b86e3dc8753426e16ae18163f615c2a2c, of the cut file here
          2104d7433b65dc49de4a215e652b6271c27371a0d2b96ff7843994769359bcf1.
  Licence: repository MIT, Copyright (c) 2024 ankandrew -> LICENSE-yolov9-plates. The weights carry no licence of
           their own; the author calls everything MIT from his side but leaves open whether YOLOv9's GPL-3.0 reaches
           exported weights (open-image-models issue #20, 2026-06-08). He trained with his fork of WongKinYiu/yolov9,
           ankandrew/yolov9 (GPL-3.0; issue #22, fast-alpr issue #47). The open questions, with sources:
           plate-detector-licensing.md.
